docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T11.md:12:This task introduces the Rust type system for the append-only event log substrate. It defines the `EventKind` enum covering all 20 spec event types, the shared `EventEnvelope` struct carrying workspace id, branch, session id, task id, actor, timestamp, stable references, payload hash, compact summary, and optional full payload location, plus the typed payload structs for each kind. Without these types, Phase 2 storage, writer, reader, and capture work has nothing to serialize. Every later phase (memory consolidation, verification, retrieval, metrics) depends on these typed records, so getting the model right now prevents downstream churn.
