docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R88.md:12:This review walks every section of the shared `definition-of-done-checklist.md` against the whole cognitive-workspace fork and certifies that each applicable item is satisfied or explicitly deferred with reason, owner, and target date per the execution philosophy in `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` ("Never defer work you can do now"). It is the second-to-last gate before R89 final readiness; passing this review means the whole-system delivery meets the cross-cutting "done means done" standard that applies regardless of which phase shipped a given artifact. Silent deferrals are not permitted — the `## Explicit Deferrals` section must either be empty (no deferrals) or list every deferral with reason, owner, and target date.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R88.md:24:1. Open `definition-of-done-checklist.md` and walk it section by section against the fork delivery. Each section below is a heading in the output file and a procedure here.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R88.md:25:2. **Workflow Completion**: Confirm every primary operator workflow works end to end. For the fork, the primary workflows are: (a) the assistant calling MCP tools to plan and apply a change; (b) the operator reviewing the memory inbox, accepting/rejecting promotions and contradictions, inspecting evidence, and triggering on-demand verification; (c) the operator deploying a new daemon binary via the runbook. Confirm both backend and operator-facing UI are complete for every user-visible workflow. Confirm background jobs (consolidation, verification, compaction) are complete.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R88.md:26:3. **Failure Handling**: Confirm validation failures return actionable errors. Confirm permission-denied is not applicable (local-first, no per-user RBAC), but workspace-boundary enforcement is verified by T83. Confirm not-found and conflict states are truthful (e.g. proposal apply on an already-applied proposal returns a clear error per T81). Confirm partial-failure behavior is defined for async paths (consolidation queue, verification jobs). Confirm UI shows loading / empty / success / failure states per R78.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R88.md:28:5. **Data Integrity and Workflow Controls**: Confirm invariants are enforced at the storage layer (foreign keys on `memory_links`, `memory_evidence`; constraints on verification status enum; uniqueness on event id). Confirm workflow statuses use explicit transition rules (verification status state machine, proposal state machine). Confirm invalid transitions are blocked and tested (T81 idempotency test).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R88.md:29:6. **Observability and Recovery**: Confirm logs and event records provide enough context to debug production failures (T82 recovery tests; T83 workspace-boundary tests emit `security` target events). Confirm critical async paths are idempotent (T81 replay-safe consolidation). Confirm recovery steps exist (T86 recovery playbook). Confirm rollback is defined (T84 migration rollback).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R88.md:32:9. **Verification Evidence**: Confirm unit, integration, and E2E coverage exists. Confirm test commands were executed and results captured (R87 hardening evidence + R79 contract round-trip evidence). Confirm manual verification was captured for UI-heavy changes (R78).
