docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T20.md:12:This task makes memory links, evidence, access history, and usefulness scores first-class records rather than columns or JSON blobs on the `memories` table. Each becomes its own table with typed Rust APIs that the rest of Phase 3 (CRUD, streams, migration, tests) and later phases (verification, retrieval, consolidation) build on. The spec is explicit that link records must carry source, target, type, strength, reason, evidence event, creator, timestamps, and verification status — none of which are expressible as denormalized columns. Without this task, contradiction and supersession cannot be queried as graph edges, retrieval cannot explain inclusion, and verification cannot recheck individual evidence anchors.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T20.md:16:> "Memory links should be first-class records: source memory, target memory or graph node, link type, strength, reason, evidence event, created by, created at, verification status."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T20.md:35:3. Define `pub struct MemoryLink { link_id: MemoryLinkId, source: MemoryId, target: MemoryLinkTarget, link_type: MemoryLinkType, strength: f32, reason: String, evidence_event_id: Option<EventId>, created_by: Actor, created_at: DateTime<Utc>, verification_status: VerificationStatus }`. `strength ∈ [0, 1]`; deny construction outside that range.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T20.md:36:4. In `memory_graph/evidence.rs`, define `pub struct MemoryEvidence { evidence_id: MemoryEvidenceId, memory_id: MemoryId, event_id: Option<EventId>, anchor: EvidenceAnchor, captured_at: DateTime<Utc>, captured_by: Actor }` where `EvidenceAnchor` is an enum over `FileSpan { file: FileId, byte_start: u64, byte_end: u64, sha256: [u8; 32] }`, `SymbolRef(SymbolId)`, `DocSection { id: DocSectionId, sha256: [u8; 32] }`, `TestResult { test: TestId, passed: bool, run_event: EventId }`, `EventReference(EventId)`. The `sha256` fields enable exact-span verification in Phase 7.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T20.md:40:   - `memory_links` columns: `link_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY`, `source_memory_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES memories(memory_id)`, `target_kind TEXT NOT NULL`, `target_id TEXT NOT NULL`, `link_type TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(link_type IN (...))`, `strength REAL NOT NULL CHECK(strength BETWEEN 0 AND 1)`, `reason TEXT NOT NULL`, `evidence_event_id INTEGER NULL`, `created_by_kind TEXT NOT NULL`, `created_by_detail TEXT NULL`, `created_at INTEGER NOT NULL`, `verification_status TEXT NOT NULL`.
