docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T01.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 0: Fork Foundation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-0-fork-foundation)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T01.md:12:This task produces the binding fork-or-extend decision that every subsequent task in this build assumes. The spec gates Phase 0 on a "fork only if necessary" rule with four named gate conditions; this document evaluates each gate condition against current Lattice code evidence, names a branch or repo, and records the decision. The decision must precede any structural change because `depends_on` chains assume the layout, crate boundaries, and migration policy that this document selects. Without an explicit, evidence-backed decision, later phases would be free to silently diverge.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T01.md:16:> "Phase 0 ends with an explicit fork/extend decision before any structural code changes begin. Fork if any of the following are true: the memory graph schema changes require breaking the existing `memories` table in a way that cannot be migrated without a full rebuild; the identity model requires changing the primary key or graph edge representation in a way that invalidates existing indexed data; the event log requires a new storage file or WAL mode incompatible with the current daemon's SQLite usage; two or more of the above apply and sharing a codebase would require sustained compatibility shims across all phases."
