docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T22.md:12:This task migrates every row from the legacy `memories` table (the 80+ column table referenced in the context inventory) into the redesigned `memories`, `memory_links`, `memory_evidence`, `memory_accesses`, and `memory_scores` tables. Migration is idempotent, restartable, audited, and verifiable: every source row produces exactly one destination memory record plus zero-or-more derived link/evidence/access rows, all with provenance back to the source row id. Without this task, Phase 3 ships a parallel schema that the daemon cannot use without losing every existing memory; with it, the substrate switches over cleanly and the Phase 0 fork-or-extend decision is honored end-to-end.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T22.md:88:- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T56.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-8-workflow-engine-v2)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T56.md:12:This task redesigns the four edit-planning workflow tools (`prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `trace_scenario`, `diagnose_failure`) on top of the Phase 1–7 substrates: unified identity, event log, memory graph, retrieval pipeline, working memory, consolidation proposals, and verification status. The redesigned tools must compose those substrates in one call so that an assistant gets a complete edit-planning bundle (code anchors, docs, tests, memory with inclusion reasons, risks, verification commands) without first issuing dozens of low-level discovery calls. This is the central deliverable of Phase 8: spec §Phase 8 DoD requires "common coding tasks require fewer manual discovery calls" and "workflows produce enough context to implement and verify changes without broad file dumping." Without this redesign, the new substrate work in Phases 1–7 stays invisible to callers.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T56.md:16:> "Phase 8 Deliverables: redesigned versions of context, change planning, scenario tracing, failure diagnosis, docs retrieval, test selection, impact analysis, and playbook generation; workflow composition over graph, event, memory, and working-memory substrates; one-call edit-planning bundles with code, docs, tests, memory, risks, and verification commands; workflow outcome recording integrated by default."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T56.md:18:> "Definition of done: common coding tasks require fewer manual discovery calls; workflows produce enough context to implement and verify changes without broad file dumping."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T56.md:24:- Dependency outputs: R55 (Phase 7 verification engine review) — verification statuses (`verified` | `unverified` | `stale` | `contradicted` | `superseded` | `expired` | `invalidated`) must be surfaced inside the bundle so stale memory cannot appear as trusted guidance per spec §Phase 7 DoD.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T56.md:35:  - Phase 7 verification engine (existence, span, scope, expiry checks).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T56.md:42:3. Implement `prepare_change` in `workflow_v2/prepare_change.rs`: classify intent via the Phase 4 classifier, resolve anchors (paths, symbols, errors, APIs, config keys) into stable identities, run hybrid candidate retrieval across graph + docs + memory + events, apply the Phase 4 scorer, then assemble a `WorkflowBundle` containing code anchors, docs sections, candidate test files (from Phase 4 ranking + `tested_by` edges), memory highlights (each carrying inclusion reason + verification status per spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles), risk notes derived from contradiction/supersession state, and verification commands (`cargo test ...`, `npm test`, etc.) inferred from the affected build targets.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T56.md:45:6. Implement `diagnose_failure` in `workflow_v2/diagnose_failure.rs`: take a stack trace, compiler error, or failing test as input, extract anchors, query `FailurePattern` memories and prior `WorkflowFailed` events for similar signatures, surface likely culprit symbols with inclusion reasons + verification status, and suggest a candidate `prepare_change` follow-up bundle handle.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T56.md:49:10. In `workflow_v2/edit_workflows_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) round-trip each tool's request/response through serde; (b) assert that `prepare_change` returns a `WorkflowBundle` with at least one ranked pivot, one memory highlight (or an explicit empty rationale), one risk note, and at least one verification command for a fixture repo; (c) assert that no memory with `verification_status = stale | contradicted | superseded | expired | invalidated` appears without an explicit stale label (spec §Phase 7 DoD); (d) assert event-emission order and hot-path budget; (e) assert `plan_edit` produces ordered steps each referencing stable identity types; (f) assert `diagnose_failure` recovers an injected fixture failure pattern.
