docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R54.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Verification Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#8-verification-engine), [§Phase 7: Verification And Freshness](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-7-verification-and-freshness), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties), [§Risks](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#risks)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R54.md:12:This task is the Phase 7 backend review. It audits T48–T53 against the spec's verification contract, the §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bullets that verification directly touches (stale surfacing, no silent broad reads), the §Risks Stale Memory Leakage and Scope Leakage controls, and the coding standard. The review must produce a verdict on whether Phase 7 is ready to ship — every later phase (Phase 8 workflow engine, Phase 10 review UI) consumes the contract surfaces this phase defines, so a failed review blocks them. A pass/fail decision without cited evidence is not a review.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R54.md:16:> Phase 7 DoD: "stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as normal trusted guidance; verification results are explainable and queryable."
