docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:12:This task delivers the two operational documents that turn the architecture suite into something an on-call human can actually use under pressure: the daily-operations runbook and the recovery playbook. The runbook is the day-in-the-life: how to deploy, how to verify health, how to read the metrics, how to respond to common alerts. The recovery playbook is the worst-day-of-the-week document: what to do when the daemon crashes, when the event log is corrupted, when memory is contradictory at scale, when migration breaks. It includes the binding deploy sequence from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy and the replay-from-snapshot procedure proved viable by T82 recovery tests.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:24:- Dependency outputs: T82 (recovery + corruption tests — provides the proven procedures), T85 (documentation suite — provides the cross-link anchors for memory/event/consolidation/retrieval/verification docs).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:27:  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/recovery_tests.rs` (from T82) — the test that exercises the replay-from-snapshot procedure this playbook documents.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:36:   - `## Daily operations` — required by verification. Cover: starting/stopping the daemon, checking health via the review panel from T76 (`consolidationQueueView`, `indexingHealthView`, `workspaceGraphHealthView`), reading the metrics report from T68/T69 (Phase 9), reviewing accepted/rejected promotions weekly.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:37:   - `## Deploy sequence` — quote the canonical sequence from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy verbatim: `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/`. Document the `sleep 2` between `pkill` and `cp` per the canonical sequence. Document the verification steps: confirm the new binary is running via `pgrep -fa lattice`; confirm the extension picks up the new binary via the activity bar.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:40:   - `## Memory hygiene` — operator weekly tasks: review promotion queue, review contradiction queue, audit stale memory, audit usefulness metrics from T68/T69.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:43:   - `## Recovery procedures` — required by verification. Cover the full recovery decision tree: daemon won't start, daemon starts but indexing fails, daemon indexing succeeds but queries return empty, queries return stale data, memory state is contradictory, snapshot file is missing or corrupted.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:44:   - `## Replay from snapshot` — required by verification. The binding procedure proved viable by T82 recovery tests. Steps: (1) stop the daemon (`pkill -f lattice`); (2) verify the snapshot file exists at `.lattice/snapshots/<latest>.snap`; (3) verify the snapshot file integrity (file size, format version header, checksum); (4) move the existing `graph.db` and `memories.db` to a quarantine location for forensics; (5) start the daemon with `--bootstrap-from-snapshot <path>`; (6) confirm the daemon emits a `SnapshotBootstrap` event; (7) confirm queries return the expected pre-snapshot state plus post-snapshot replay; (8) document the post-recovery audit checklist. Cross-link to the test `test_replay_from_snapshot_reconstructs_state` in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/recovery_tests.rs`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:45:   - `## Replay from event log only` — fallback procedure when no snapshot is usable. Steps and post-replay verification.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:47:   - `## Corruption recovery` — per-class procedures matching the T82 corruption test scenarios: corrupted payload, mismatched hash, invalid kind, invalid stable reference, truncated file, snapshot version mismatch.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:71:- Single source of truth: the deploy sequence is quoted from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` exactly once; the runbook references the source rather than fork its own copy.
