docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Measurable Success Criteria](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#measurable-success-criteria)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:12:This task ships the regression tests that prove the cognitive workspace fork beats the baselines on every initial target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria. The tests run the redesigned tools (T56/T57) against the T66 fixture repos, feed the captured events into the T65 metrics collector, render the T68 regression report, and assert each spec §Measurable Success Criteria target. Without this task, the metrics infrastructure exists but no automated gate proves the system meets its stated goals — the Phase 9 DoD ("changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote") would not be satisfied.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:16:> "Initial targets: 30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks; 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads; 80 percent memory inclusion precision on curated memory benchmarks; zero trusted display of known contradicted memory; zero trusted display of known stale memory without stale label; 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks." (spec §Measurable Success Criteria)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:20:> "The fork should beat current Lattice on: lower tool calls per coding task; lower irrelevant context inclusion; higher relevant file/symbol recall; higher memory reuse precision; lower stale memory surfacing; better repeated-failure avoidance; better test recommendation accuracy; better user correction retention; faster diagnosis from failures; more explainable context selection." (spec §Measurable Success Criteria)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:30:  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json` (from T04) — baseline column for delta-based assertions (30% fewer, 40% fewer).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:38:2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/regression_tests.rs` containing one `#[test]` per spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target. Each test loads the T66 fixtures, runs the redesigned tools end-to-end against the golden tasks, feeds events into the T65 `MetricsCollector`, and asserts the corresponding threshold using the T68 `SuccessCriteriaThresholds`:
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:41:   - `test_memory_inclusion_precision_at_least_80pct` — `MemoryInclusionPrecision` ≥ 0.80 on the curated memory benchmark tasks from T66.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:42:   - `test_zero_trusted_display_of_contradicted_memory` — `ContradictionMissedRate` equals 0 across all fixture tasks.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:43:   - `test_zero_trusted_display_of_stale_memory_without_label` — `StaleMemorySurfacedRate` equals 0 across all fixture tasks (stale memories may appear, but never without an explicit stale label per spec §Phase 7 DoD).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:44:   - `test_relevant_test_recommendation_at_least_90pct` — `TestsRecommendedVsNeeded` recall ≥ 0.90 on the curated tasks from T66.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T69.md:46:4. Mark long-running tests `#[ignore]` only if they exceed CI budget; the verification command runs with `-- --include-ignored` so CI executes them. Spec §Tests as documentation forbids silently skipping required coverage.
