docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:12:This task delivers the memory inbox — the operator's primary list view over every memory the daemon knows about. It mounts inside the review panel scaffolding from T71, lists memories with filterable columns (status, scope, class), and renders one status badge per row covering all eight verification states from spec §Verification Engine. The inbox is the entry point operators use to find the memory they want to verify, accept, reject, or inspect — without it, the promotion queue (T73), contradiction queue (T73), stale view (T74), and evidence inspector (T74) have nothing to link to. Spec §10 lists "memory inbox" first among the required operator views, which fixes its position as the spine of the review surface.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:20:> "Each memory record requires: stable id; content; memory class; assertion type; scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization; verification status; confidence and confidence reason; freshness policy; ... last verified state." (spec §4 — drives the filter axes)
