docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R89.md:12:This is the final gate before the cognitive-workspace fork is declared shippable. It assembles three matrices that each prior review touched only locally: (1) spec coverage matrix — one row per spec §Phase asserting PASS/PASS-WITH-CAVEATS/BLOCK; (2) measurable success criteria matrix — one row per target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets, with the evidence file path proving the target was hit; (3) risk controls matrix — one row per risk from spec §Risks asserting the control is implemented and pointing to the artifact that proves it. The review concludes with a single binding `## Ship verdict`: PASS or BLOCK. The verification step runs the full daemon test workspace and the full extension build to confirm the system compiles, lints, tests, and ships clean from a fresh checkout.
