docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:1:# T51 — Phase 7 — Time-bound expiry + incremental verification triggered by graph changes
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Verification Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#8-verification-engine), [§Phase 7: Verification And Freshness](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-7-verification-and-freshness)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:12:This task ships two spec-required Phase 7 mechanisms. First, time-bound expiry: memories with an `expires_at` reach the `expired` state automatically when their timestamp passes, and the verifier emits the corresponding `MarkExpired` proposal. Second, incremental verification: the verifier walks only memories whose evidence cites files/symbols that actually changed since the last graph snapshot, never a full rescan. The spec is explicit that "large repos cannot tolerate full rescans for every memory" — this is the mechanism that makes Phase 7 scalable.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:22:> Phase 7 DoD: "stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as normal trusted guidance; verification results are explainable and queryable."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:26:- Dependency outputs: T48 (verifier core + `verification_jobs`), T49 (span validation), T50 (scope enforcement). Incremental verification dispatches to all three.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:37:1. Read spec §Verification Engine "Verification checks" + "Verification outputs" + the incremental constraint. Copy verbatim into the top-of-file doc comments on `verification/expiry.rs` and `verification/incremental.rs`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:38:2. In `verification/expiry.rs`, implement `ExpiryScanner::scan(workspace_id, now: DateTime<Utc>) -> ExpiryReport`. Query memories with `expires_at IS NOT NULL AND expires_at <= ? AND verification_status != 'expired'`. For each match, emit a `MarkExpired` proposal through the T39 runtime carrying `prior_state.expires_at` and `proposed_state.verification_status = 'expired'`. Idempotent: re-running on a memory already `expired` is a no-op.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:40:4. In `verification/incremental.rs`, implement `IncrementalVerifier::on_graph_delta(prior_snapshot_id, new_snapshot_id, changed_files: Vec<FileId>)`. Algorithm: (a) compute the set of changed symbols by intersecting changed files with the graph's `Contains` edges from Phase 1, (b) query `memory_evidence` for every memory citing any changed file or symbol, (c) dispatch each impacted memory through `VerifierCore::verify_memory` (T48 + T49 + T50 in sequence — existence, span, scope), (d) update `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id` on memories whose verdict is now `Verified`, (e) return an `IncrementalReport { impacted, verified, stale, invalidated, expired, elapsed }`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:44:8. Update memory rows on successful verification: bump `last_verified_at = now` and `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id = new_snapshot_id` via T39 proposals (`Refresh` kind from T41) — never direct writes.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:45:9. In `verification/incremental_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) a graph delta touching file `F` causes only memories whose evidence cites `F` (or symbols contained in `F`) to be re-verified; memories citing unrelated files are NOT scanned (assert via a counting test seam), (b) the `ExpiryScanner` flips `expires_at <= now` memories to `expired` via a `MarkExpired` proposal and is idempotent on re-run, (c) `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id` advances on success, (d) a memory whose evidence cites a deleted file goes from `verified` → `invalidated` on the next delta, (e) `IncrementalVerifier` respects the bounded work budget — given 1000 impacted memories and a budget of 50, exactly 50 are processed and the remainder is re-enqueued.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:49:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/expiry.rs` — `ExpiryScanner::scan`, `MarkExpired` proposal emission, idempotence.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:50:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/incremental.rs` — `IncrementalVerifier::on_graph_delta`, change-set narrowing, bounded work budget, snapshot-id bump on success.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:51:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/incremental_tests.rs` — incremental-scope narrowing, expiry idempotence, budget enforcement, snapshot-id propagation.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:55:- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/expiry.rs` — confirms the expiry module exists.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:56:- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/incremental.rs` — confirms the incremental module exists.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:57:- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib verification::incremental_tests` — every expiry + incremental unit test passes.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:63:- Single source of truth: per-memory verification routes through `VerifierCore::verify_memory` (T48); state writes route through T39 proposals; no parallel paths.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md:68:- Observability: `tracing::info_span!("incremental_verification", workspace_id, prior_snapshot, new_snapshot, impacted, verified, stale, invalidated, expired, elapsed_ms)`.
