docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T19.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Memory Graph](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#4-memory-graph)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T19.md:12:This task replaces the legacy single-table memory model with a typed memory schema that the rest of Phase 3 builds on. It defines the full memory-class taxonomy (including `CounterMemory` as a first-class class distinct from a `contradicts` link), the SQLite DDL covering every spec-required memory field, the Rust types that mirror the schema, and an architecture doc that records the model authoritatively so later phases (retrieval, consolidation, verification) reference one source of truth. Without this redesign, memory cannot represent claims, evidence, validity conditions, or counter-claims — only loose notes — which violates the spec's core thesis.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T19.md:16:> "Primary memory classes: `Observation`, `Decision`, `Constraint`, `Pattern`, `AntiPattern`, `WorkflowOutcome`, `FailurePattern`, `Procedure`, `Preference`, `ArchitectureInvariant`, `DocsContract`, `OpenQuestion`, `CounterMemory` — a memory record that explicitly asserts a prior memory is wrong or no longer applicable. Distinct from a `contradicts` link: a link connects two existing memories; a CounterMemory is a first-class record authored by an agent or user that carries its own evidence, scope, and verification status and can itself be superseded or invalidated."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T19.md:18:> "Each memory record requires: stable id, content, memory class, assertion type, scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization, verification status, confidence and confidence reason, freshness policy, validity conditions, invalidation triggers, provenance events, evidence references, linked files, linked symbols, linked docs, linked tests, linked memories, contradiction links, supersession links, access history, usefulness scores, last verified state."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T19.md:39:8. Define `pub struct InvalidationTrigger { kind: TriggerKind, target: StableRef }` so verification (Phase 7) can subscribe deterministically: `TriggerKind = { FileChanged, SymbolChanged, DocSectionChanged, TestFailed, TimeExpired }`.
