docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T30.md:41:3. Implement one pure-function evaluator per signal in `scoring.rs`, each ≤50 lines, each returning a `SignalScore` with both score and reason. The thirteen evaluators are: `task_type_compatibility`, `graph_proximity`, `exact_identifier_match`, `semantic_similarity`, `verification_status`, `freshness`, `scope`, `evidence_strength`, `contradiction_or_supersession_state`, `past_usefulness`, `recent_successful_reuse`, `user_preference_compatibility`, `token_cost`. Each MUST be present; missing data yields a score of 0 and a reason like `"no <field> available; signal skipped"`, never a panic or silent skip.
