docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Verification Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#8-verification-engine), [§Phase 7: Verification And Freshness](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-7-verification-and-freshness)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:12:This task implements the second verification check from spec §Verification Engine: when a memory's evidence captured an exact text span (a byte range or `(start_line, end_line)`) at the time of creation, verification must confirm the current file content at that span still matches what was captured. If it does not, the verifier emits a `MarkStale` proposal (the assertion may still be true but the citation is stale) or `MarkInvalidated` (the evidence is gone). This is the difference between "the file still exists" (T48) and "what the memory said about the file is still backed by the same bytes." It is the load-bearing mechanism for the spec's §Stale Memory Leakage risk control.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:24:- Dependency outputs: T48 — `VerifierCore`, `VerificationStatus`, `VerificationVerdict`, `verification_jobs` schema. Span validation slots in as one more check kind alongside existence.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:29:  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/existence.rs` (T48) — pattern for one-check-per-evidence-row.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:34:1. Read spec §Verification Engine "Verification checks" list. Copy the span-validation bullet verbatim into the top-of-file doc comment on `verification/spans.rs`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:36:3. In `verification/spans.rs`, implement `SpanValidator::validate(evidence: &MemoryEvidence, current_file_bytes: &[u8]) -> VerificationVerdict`. Algorithm: (a) if `evidence.span` is `None`, return `Verified` (this check is no-op for evidence without an exact span — the existence check from T48 already covered the file), (b) if `byte_end > current_file_bytes.len()`, return `VerificationVerdict { status: Stale, reason: "FileShrunkBelowSpan" }`, (c) compute SHA-256 of `current_file_bytes[byte_start..byte_end]` and compare to `evidence.evidence_content_hash`; equal → `Verified`, unequal → `Stale { reason: ContentChanged }`, (d) handle encoding-mismatch (BOM appearance/removal, CRLF/LF flip) explicitly by recording `EncodingChanged` so the surfacing layer in T52 can distinguish noise from substantive change.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:38:5. Provide a streaming read path: do NOT read the whole file when only a small span needs verifying. Use the existing storage layer's `read_range(file_id, start, end)` (or add one if absent, in the same task) so verification stays cheap on large files.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:39:6. Persist span-mismatch details: extend the verification-jobs `reason` column to carry a structured JSON payload `{ "kind": "SpanMismatch", "subkind": "ContentChanged" | "FileShrunkBelowSpan" | "EncodingChanged" | "FileMissing", "evidence_id": <id> }` so the Phase 10 inbox UI can render the exact reason.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:41:8. In `verification/spans_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) unchanged content at the span returns `Verified`, (b) modified content at the span returns `Stale { ContentChanged }`, (c) file truncated below `byte_end` returns `Stale { FileShrunkBelowSpan }`, (d) CRLF↔LF flip is reported as `EncodingChanged`, not `ContentChanged`, (e) evidence with `span = None` returns `Verified` (no-op), (f) span validation never reads the whole file (assert via a tracing-instrumented mock storage that counts bytes read).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:45:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/spans.rs` — `EvidenceSpan`, `SpanMismatch`, `SpanValidator::validate`, streaming-range read path, structured-reason emission.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:46:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/spans_tests.rs` — unchanged / modified / truncated / encoding-flip / no-span / no-whole-file-read coverage.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:50:- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/spans.rs` — confirms the spans module exists.
