docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T61.md:12:This task produces the audited final MCP tool surface for the cognitive workspace fork: an audit doc recording which tools were collapsed and why, and the canonical reference doc enumerating every tool the daemon ships, its render modes, expansion handles, budget controls, deprecation status, and shim policy. Spec §MCP Surface "Tool surface discipline" makes this audit binding: "ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients … The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract." Without this task, the Phase 8 work ships an unaudited surface and Phase 9 metrics regress against the wrong set of tool names.
