docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T59.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§MCP Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#9-mcp-surface)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T59.md:12:This task introduces the unified `verify_explain_memory` MCP tool (collapsing the spec's `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` per §MCP Surface "Tool surface discipline") and the new `list_memory_conflicts` tool. The unified tool runs verification checks against a memory and returns both the resulting status (`verified` | `unverified` | `in_review` | `stale` | `contradicted` | `superseded` | `expired` | `invalidated`) and a structured explanation of why each linked file/symbol/doc/test contributed to that status. `list_memory_conflicts` surfaces all contradiction and supersession edges anchored on a target memory or graph node so an operator can review them. Both tools are required by spec §MCP Surface and are the trust surface for the verification engine — without them, the Phase 7 verifier produces statuses that no assistant or operator can interrogate.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T59.md:22:> "Every memory-bearing response should identify: why the memory was included; evidence strength; verification status; freshness status; contradiction/supersession state; scope; expansion target." (spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T59.md:26:- Dependency outputs: R55 (Phase 7 verification engine review) — `verify_explain_memory` is the MCP surface for the Phase 7 verifier; its outputs must match the Phase 7 status taxonomy exactly.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T59.md:28:  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/` — Phase 7 verifier (existence, span, scope, expiry checks; incremental verification jobs).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T59.md:39:2. Implement `verify_explain_memory` in `memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` as the unified tool. Accept `memory_id: MemoryId` plus optional `mode: "verify" | "explain" | "verify_and_explain"` (default `verify_and_explain`). Internally run the Phase 7 verifier on the memory, then construct an `ExplainReport` that itemizes each verification check (linked file exists, linked symbol exists, cited doc exists, linked test exists, evidence span still matches, contradiction state coherent, scope leak absent, time-bound expiry honored) and the outcome per check. Return a `VerifyExplainResponse` with `status: VerificationStatus`, `checks: Vec<CheckResult>` (each carrying `kind`, `target`, `outcome`, `evidence_ref`), `confidence_delta`, and an `expansion_handle` so the caller can pull richer context.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T59.md:40:3. Mode semantics: `verify` returns only the status + a minimal summary; `explain` skips re-running checks and returns the last persisted `ExplainReport`; `verify_and_explain` runs verification and returns the freshly-derived `ExplainReport`. Default is `verify_and_explain` because spec §Verification Engine and §MCP Tool Contract Principles together require fresh, explainable status on every memory surface.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T59.md:41:4. Implement `list_memory_conflicts` in `memory_v2/list_memory_conflicts.rs`. Accept `anchor: MemoryId | FileId | SymbolId | DocSectionId`, traverse `contradicts` and `supersedes` link types from Phase 3 memory_links, and return a paginated list of `ConflictRecord`s each carrying `source`, `target`, `link_type` (`contradicts` | `supersedes`), `link_strength`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `link_verification_status`, and `reason`. Honor scope filters per spec §Risks "Scope Leakage."
