docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T74.md:12:This task delivers the stale-memory view and the evidence inspector, plus the on-demand verification trigger that calls the Phase 8 `verify_memory` tool. The stale view is the operator's lever to see every memory whose linked files, symbols, docs, or tests have drifted; the evidence inspector is the deep-dive surface for any single memory (used both from the inbox in T72 and the stale view here); and the verification trigger lets an operator re-run verification on demand instead of waiting for the background verifier. Together they implement the human-side control for spec §Stale Memory Leakage: "agents trust outdated memory; control: freshness indexes, graph-change-triggered verification, stale labels in all memory surfaces, and tests that stale memory cannot rank as trusted."
